  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MECS scale-up in Tanzania via Loughborough University</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale-up of MECS programme activities in Tanzania via Loughborough University and partners, including: development of supply chains for the distribution of 8,000 electric pressure cookers in urban and rural areas where charcoal is still the primary source of cooking fuel; development and implementation of a government-stamped nationwide campaign to increase awareness and demand for electric cooking expected to reach 10% of the population; provision of training to 300 technicians on repair and maintenance of electric cooking appliances; and support to 20 schools to transition to modern energy cooking.</narrative>
  </description>
